{"chunk_id": "e8abeee239e6", "text": "This section recounts the climactic fulfillment of Narada\u2019s prophecy about Satyavan\u2019s death. Knowing the destined day, Savitri undertakes a severe three\u2011night fast and accompanies her husband into the forest despite her dread. While cutting wood, Satyavan collapses and dies with his head in her lap. Yama, the god of death, appears and takes Satyavan\u2019s soul. Refusing to abandon her husband, Savitri follows Yama and engages him in profound discourse on righteousness, devotion, and moral duty. Impressed by her wisdom and fidelity, Yama grants several boons: the restoration of her father\u2011in\u2011law\u2019s sight and kingdom, sons for her father, and a hundred sons for herself. Realizing that the last boon requires Satyavan\u2019s life, Yama restores him. The episode highlights the power of steadfast virtue, intelligence, and marital devotion to overcome even death.\nSavitri follows Yama after Satyavan\u2019s death, wins multiple boons through wisdom and devotion, and ultimately secures Satyavan\u2019s life.\nThemes: devotion and fidelity, death and destiny, righteous speech, power of vows, boons and divine justice", "vector": [0.005185225047171116, -0.03561995550990105, -0.0104628661647439, 0.010502473451197147, -0.004508604295551777, 0.022945692762732506, -0.014694221317768097, -0.016991430893540382, -0.02412070333957672, -0.015459957532584667, 0.026906399056315422, 0.024450762197375298, 0.01870773732662201, 0.004960784688591957, -0.006924635265022516, 0.00687182554975152, 0.05188525468111038, -0.0017856184858828783, 0.03876211494207382, -0.029810916632413864, 0.01233760081231594, 0.0011593317613005638, -0.008139251731336117, 0.01993555575609207, -0.010284634307026863, 0.01137382909655571, 0.01872093975543976, -0.0334547683596611, 0.015393946319818497, -0.013057129457592964, -0.019196223467588425, -0.01953948475420475, -0.008192061446607113, -0.032847460359334946, -0.01542035024613142, 0.010971156880259514,